WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.178
The four-stage embedded family shows why suffixes matter.

2
00:00:04.178 --> 00:00:11.433
CV32E40P preserves RI5CY and PULP lineage and may include F or Zfinx plus PULP custom instructions.

3
00:00:11.433 --> 00:00:19.275
CV32E40X exposes CORE-V-XIF, allowing external modules to implement instructions without changing core RTL.

4
00:00:19.275 --> 00:00:28.436
CV32E40S targets security systems, with Machine and User privilege support, enhanced protection, and anti-tampering features.

5
00:00:28.436 --> 00:00:36.425
The shared prefix predicts width, class, and pipeline; the suffix points to a different integration contract.

